t with American presidents - all  of a sudden  as president of the United States he  talks about a little Rokit man he talks  about a bloody nose strike and next  thing you know everything changes and  Kim jong-un wants to meet with Donald  Trump but that's what the trumpets and  Trump himself seemed to be missing over  the entire weekend which is that North  Korea under Kim jong-un under Kim  jong-il they've always wanted to meet in  person with an American president it's  the u.s. who has chosen not to do it  unless there were some preconditions  imposed concessions agreed to by the  North Korean side it's not newsworthy at  all that Kim jong-un wants to meet with  Donald Trump  the newsworthy part would be the  American policy change of Trump meeting  with Kim jong-un with no preconditions  and so immediately the White House  started walking all of this back and our  favorite press secretary Sarah Huckabee  Sanders told reporters a couple days ago  that actually no Trump is not just going  to show up and meet with Kim jong-un  there need to be concrete concessions  made beforehand and you'll notice this  is a basically completely opposed  situation a different situation than  what the headlines were claiming this  will be any more than a photo-op Kim  jong-un gets his equal footing in his  view on the world stage with a leader in  the free world I definitely don't think  that the president's getting nothing  when we've already said and frankly I've  said it many times since walking in here  in the last 10 minutes that the  president will not have the meeting  without seeing concrete steps and  concrete actions take place by North  Korea so the president would actually be  getting something and frankly the world  would be getting something if we can get  to a place where North Korea is  denuclearizing it is a massive step and  it's something that will make the entire  globe much safer and even president moon  has said that this is because of the  leadership of President Trump that's  right so after all the headlines and all  the tweets from the the trumpets about  Trump the hero the real situation is  that the American president is willing  to consider meeting with Kim jong-un  only with preconditions and  concessions which is exactly the old  policy nothing has changed that has been  the situation for a very long time in  the United States before Trump North  Korean leaders wanted to meet with  American presidents and American  presidents were only willing to consider  that if North Korea made concessions  before the meeting which they've not  been willing to do and now during Trump  it's the exact same same scenario so  Trump shot his mouth off because he  believed that it was notable that Kim  jong-un wanted to meet with him when it  was not that's really the funniest part  of all of this when the headlines broke  the trumpets thought that this was major  and also some of them thought that this  meant Kim jong-un was ready to disarm  that wanting a meeting with Trump met  Kim jong-un was ready to meet and say  I'm giving up my nukes Kim jong-un has  no interest in giving up his nukes he  wants to meet with president Trump to  convey power that he got a meeting with  Trump and he'll know that if he gets the  meeting it would be because he has the  nukes and people are afraid of how we  might use them the last thing that Kim  jong-un is going to do is meet with  Trump to get rid of the nukes and you've  got to put yourself in his shoes right  if you're in the situation of Kim  jong-un in North Korea Kim jong-un knows  that the nukes are hugely important as a  bargaining chip and this also applies to  newer reports from the last few hours  that Kim jong-un wants a peace treaty  with the United States this by some on  the trumpets right is being reported as  look at what Kim jong-un is willing to  do for Trump Kim jong-un has always  wanted others to do for them things and  that's what this is it's not take my  nukes and nothing bad will happen it's  we want the u.s. to agree to X Y Z more  than likely that would include a formal  end to the Korean War which from the  point of view of Kim jong-un would  necessitate the total removal of all US  forces from South Korea which is not  going to happen so listen I'm not saying  this is a bad idea I would love for the  United States to reduce its military  footprint around the world I would love  for there to be action  will productive disarmament talks with  North Korea but the fantasy that Trump  achieved something big and that Kim  jong-un is just willing to give  everything up now because of the power  of Donald Trump it is an absolute and  total fantasy yeah I'm a little  disappointed because it doesn't seem  like this meeting is going to happen  after all no and I think only good can  come from this meeting right you have  two people sitting at a table together  we know that Trump is good schmoozer and  he can wine and dine Kim jong-un and  maybe they'll both come out of it  feeling better are you  is that tongue-in-cheek or is that for  real no I really think that I remember  Obama during the campaign in 2008 yeah  about how he would meet with Iran  without precondition yep is it so bad if  Trump does it with kim jong hoon i think  the difference is if you get to  megalomaniacs  who do have access to nuclear weapons  together in a room with each other when  one of those megalomaniacs also knows  nothing about anything I think it's a  recipe for disaster I think the way that  this need if you're gonna do this  seriously right if you're gonna do this  seriously what you have to do is say  great we're going to have a North Korean  US summit probably with South Korean  officials as well and maybe even other  allies and they are going to really do  the bulk of the actual negotiation  without the megalomaniacs in the room  and then once we come to what will be in  principle and agreement we will have  something more ceremonial for Trump and  